# ARK Workspace Rules

- Repair order workflow is the primary operational surface.
- The workspace should feel calm under pressure.
- Main flow owns entry, editing, recommendations, estimate lines, and operational interaction.
- Right rail owns context only: customer, vehicle, status, and totals.
- Bottom actions own workflow pacing: save draft, convert estimate, approve, print later.
- Avoid stacking sidebars, panels, widgets, tabs, metrics, and forms.
- Prefer one coherent operational surface over many widgets.
- Operational context should remain visible beside workflow actions.
- Totals must have one authoritative calculation path.
- Avoid modal-heavy workflows.
- Keyboard and search speed matter more than animations.
- Workflow continuity is more important than visual density.
- Every added UI element must reduce operational friction.
- Freeze layout expansion unless there is clear operational pain.
- Improve interaction quality before adding more visible structure.
